   "text": {
    "L1": "Heat from the Sun reaches Earth by radiation. Radiation does not need material in between, so it can cross empty space.",
    "L2": "That is why the belief that heat cannot travel through empty space is wrong.",
    "L3": "We also feel radiation from the side of a heater or a hot stove without touching it.",
    "L4": "Every object gives out some radiation. Hotter objects give out more.",
    "L5": "Dark and dull surfaces absorb more radiation, so they heat faster in sunlight.",
    "L6": "Light-coloured and shiny surfaces reflect more radiation and stay cooler. That is why light clothes are comfortable in summer.",
    "L7": "A black solar cooker absorbs sunlight, while white roofs and silver tanks reflect more and stay cooler."
   },
